# Diamond prices: diamonds

```elixir
Mix.install([
  {:giggly, path: Path.join(__DIR__, "..")},
  {:kino, "~> 0.19"}
  ])
```

## About this notebook

ggplot2's reference page for [`diamonds`](https://ggplot2.tidyverse.org/reference/diamonds.html)
has no examples, so this notebook says only what the page describes and where Giggly stands.

`diamonds` holds the prices and other attributes of almost 54,000 round cut diamonds: price in US
dollars, weight in carats, the quality of the cut, colour from D (best) to J (worst), clarity,
length, width and depth in millimetres, the total depth as a percentage of the mean of length and
width, and the width of the top relative to the widest point. Giggly has it as
`Giggly.Datasets.diamonds/0`, a keyword list of columns `Giggly.Plot.new/2` takes as it is. The
cut, colour and clarity are ordered factors, `Giggly.Factor`s with R's levels, so a plot orders
them as R does, the cut from Fair to Ideal.
